Appendix C: Detailed Proof of Lemma 1 (Uniform Approximate Optimality)

C.1 Statement

Let  T^\dagger = \arg\max_{T \in [0,T_{\max}]} J(T|X)  be the true optimal meditation budget, and let  T^* = \arg\max_{T \in [0,T_{\max}]} [\widehat{V}(\mathcal{M}_T(X)) - \lambda C(T)]  be the estimated optimum. Under Assumption A5, with probability at least  1-\delta :

J(T^*|X) \ge J(T^\dagger|X) - 2\varepsilon.

C.2 Proof

Define the estimated net utility:

\widehat{J}(T|X) = \widehat{V}(\mathcal{M}_T(X)) - V(X) - \lambda C(T).

By definition of  T^* , for all  T \in [0,T_{\max}] :

\widehat{J}(T^*|X) \ge \widehat{J}(T|X).

In particular, for  T = T^\dagger :

\widehat{J}(T^*|X) \ge \widehat{J}(T^\dagger|X).

From Assumption A5, on the event where  \sup_T |\widehat{V}(\mathcal{M}_T(X)) - V(\mathcal{M}_T(X))| \le \varepsilon  holds (which has probability at least  1-\delta ), we have for all  T :

|J(T|X) - \widehat{J}(T|X)| = |V(\mathcal{M}_T(X)) - \widehat{V}(\mathcal{M}_T(X))| \le \varepsilon.

Therefore:

J(T^*|X) \ge \widehat{J}(T^*|X) - \varepsilon \ge \widehat{J}(T^\dagger|X) - \varepsilon \ge J(T^\dagger|X) - 2\varepsilon.

The chain of inequalities holds on the event of probability at least  1-\delta , completing the proof. ∎

C.3 Discussion of Tightness

The bound is tight in the worst case: if the estimator is maximally pessimistic at  T^\dagger  (error  -\varepsilon ) and maximally optimistic at  T^*  (error  +\varepsilon ), then the gap  J(T^\dagger) - J(T^*)  can be as large as  2\varepsilon . The factor 2 is unavoidable without additional assumptions on the correlation structure of estimator errors.

